\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A link on a one-site torus}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{On the one-site free torus, every difference in the
counting operator of \ref{fdip-00OL} vanishes. A coefficient link on
that same cellular loop still transports its fiber.
The [based-link convention](fdip-00SH) retains this loop as a
label even though its endpoints coincide. Which right
multiplications continue to commute when that link is allowed
to vary?}
